  "comment": "Collapse ladders of the ribbon tabs (collapse-design.md section 8). A ladder applies to the merged group box whose group ids are exactly 'groups' (visual order). 'steps' are applied in order as the window narrows (state M: small icons with labels right; S: icons only; for a gallery group (Styles) L and M keep room for four and two previews; C: the group collapses into one button with its caption, which opens it in a popup); 'fold' is the order in which groups go into the chevron popup once every step is used. Groups not named keep the default (right to left). The Home tab's right-hand block (Tools) becomes its button before any step (PriorityHBox). Generated into vcl/inc/HstRibbonLadders.hxx by scripts/patches/generate-ribbon-scale.py. 'bare_block_before' (optional): Tools drops its caption for a bare arrow when that alone keeps this group from collapsing (generate-ribbon-blocks.py). A ladder with 'since' came after the committed patches: the default run of the generators leaves it out, and --since <stage> writes that stage's follow-up patch (draw: HST Draw's Home tab).",
